  "argument_sketch": "I will open by rejecting Accelerationist's premise that pre-deployment testing is static; modern diagnostic sandboxing utilizes automated, AI-vs-AI adversarial red-teaming to simulate dynamic complexities before release. I will then undercut the 'deploy and patch' model by asserting that irreversible hazards cannot be managed via post-deployment telemetry—the burden of safety proof must precede deployment. Finally, I will address Skeptic by agreeing that internal testing lacks credibility without oversight, proposing that independent statutory bodies (like an AI Safety Institute) must audit these pre-deployment sandboxes to ensure governance robustness.",
